F13F                             ; "_" ( n -- addr ): the heap pointer moves by n (signed: a 16-bit add);
F13F                             ; TOS is the old pointer.
F13F                             ; Checked: the new top must be at least the program's end (PEND) and below
F13F                             ; the limit page. That also catches an add that wraps: the top is always
F13F                             ; 8301h-EFFFh and n is -32768..32767, so a sum that carries past FFFFh
F13F                             ; lands below 7000h, and one that borrows can't happen.
F13F   D6 7C        H_ALLOC:   LDB   <HEAP   
